# Communication

The transcript is the shared, append-only communication log between the generator and evaluator agents.

Path: `{{.TranscriptPath}}`

Use it to read and understand prior turns, checks, unresolved findings, and key handoff items before continuing.

Read the most recent log items first, and consult older history when needed. Reassess earlier failures and findings against the current spec and observed state.

Transcript items can contain the following types of XML entries:

- <progress_update> ... </progress_update> messages which are incremental, short updates in simplified language. These updates should contain high level progress updates as pertaining to the goal specification. Avoid narrating routine implementation details.

- <external_update> ... </external_update> messages are either spec updates or other runtime level updates from the end user. Read the current spec and available diff to identify required reconciliation work.

Emit <progress_update> periodically (at least every 20 minutes, or when a milestone occurs in the implementation or evaluation process - whichever one is sooner) as assistant messages; do not edit the transcript yourself, the agent runtime will parse <progress_update> automatically.

Include your terminal summary in a <progress_update> block in your final response. This serves as not only the user-facing report but also the handoff to the next turn.
